Package: raye-wine
Architecture: amd64
# The layer comes in parts so that no single package grows past what the
# archive mirrors take (GitHub refuses files of 100 MB). They always move
# together: each part is pinned to this exact version.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         raye-wine-i386 (= ${binary:Version}),
         raye-wine-mono (= ${binary:Version}),
         raye-wine-gecko (= ${binary:Version}),
         raye-wine-gecko-i386 (= ${binary:Version}),
         raye-wine-extras (= ${binary:Version}),
         libcups2t64, libdbus-1-3, libegl1, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6,
         libgl1, libgnutls30t64, libv4l-0t64, libva2, libva-drm2, libvulkan1,
         libx11-6, libxcomposite1, libxcursor1, libxext6, libxfixes3, libxi6,
         libxinerama1, libxkbregistry0, libxrandr2, libxrender1, libxxf86vm1,
         pipewire-jack, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
         gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly, gstreamer1.0-libav
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers, pipewire-pulse, libsdl2-2.0-0, fonts-liberation
Description: Raye's layer for Windows programs
 The layer that runs Windows programs on Raye, kept in /opt/raye-wine so
 it never clashes with another one on the system. 64-bit and 32-bit
 programs run without any 32-bit system library.
 .
 Every new space gets Direct3D 8 to 12 on Vulkan (DXVK and VKD3D-Proton),
 with the builtin OpenGL renderer when the computer has no usable Vulkan,
 .NET and web views built in, sound through PipeWire, and
 the kernel's ntsync. Nothing is downloaded when a program starts.
 Programs that read the screen (DXGI duplication, GDI) get the desktop
 through the Raye share picker and PipeWire.

